# main-frecuencia-dseg: the firmware's main screen with the frequency row and the
# clock drawn with the segmented-digit (seven-segment LCD) family — the
# "Casio-watch" panel of decision 1 / issue #9.
#
# It is the sample screen of the digit families (src/fonts/font_families.h,
# `font_digit()`): the same main screen as home-usb-20m, only the family of the
# digit panels changes (freq_style/freq_main_style = sony_30/sony_38 and the two
# clock labels, src/styles.c and src/clock.c). Everything else — every letter, the
# buttons, the dialogs — keeps the default family: a segmented face has no
# lowercase and its letters are approximations, so it is never a whole-family
# choice.
#
# The unlit-segment look (a ghost "8" behind the digit at low alpha) is NOT drawn:
# the firmware has no such layer, and adding one is a rendering feature of its own
# (see docs/fonts-spec.md, PENDIENTES). What this fixture shows is the real thing:
# the digits of the frequency row and the clock set in the segmented face.
#
# The rest of the candidates are measured with `--font` (every screen); the digit
# families are measured on this fixture (see tools/fonts/README.md).

name main-frecuencia-dseg
screen main

seed 20

digits dseg7

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode usb
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
